.TH SDL_NOLONGLONG 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_NOLONGLONG \- Don\(aqt let SDL use \(dqlong long\(dq C types.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_NOLONGLONG 1
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL will define this if it believes the compiler doesn\(aqt understand the \(dqlong long\(dq syntax for C datatypes\[char46] This can happen on older compilers\[char46]
.PP
If _your_ compiler doesn\(aqt support \(dqlong long\(dq but SDL doesn\(aqt know it, it is safe to define this yourself to build against the SDL headers\[char46]
.PP
If this is defined, it will remove access to some C runtime support functions, like
.BR SDL_ulltoa
and
.BR SDL_strtoll
that refer to this datatype explicitly\[char46] The rest of SDL will still be available\[char46]
.PP
SDL\(aqs own source code cannot be built with a compiler that has this defined, for various technical reasons\[char46]

